  "name": "senpi-strategy-discover",
  "description": "Find the Senpi template that best fits the user's idea, as the BASE of their own strategy: they fork it and make it theirs (a lever shifted, a rule of their own) before it goes live. Called by senpi-strategy-author to find a base for a thesis, and directly when the user asks to browse (\"show me your templates\", \"a ready-made fund\") or names a template. Strategy asks (\"what should I trade?\", \"recommend a strategy\", \"trade for me\") start in senpi-strategy-author, which runs this first; one that names stocks or coins (\"a basket like Apple, Microsoft and Nvidia\") is still a strategy ask, answered with templates, never with research on the assets. Every pick deploys as `<User>'s <Template>` (or a name of their own) after ops walks them through it. You talk and RANK (their worldview as `--theme`); a hidden engine (scripts/discover.py) fetches data + filters. NOT for installing a NAMED strategy (senpi-strategy-ops) or building one (senpi-strategy-author).",
